{
  "lemmas": [
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_1; @(posedge clk) s_nexttime ((vol <= N) && (sig == (vol == N))); endproperty",
      "explanation": "After any clock transition, vol is bounded by the clamp, and sig is high exactly when vol equals N. The one-clock shift avoids assuming a power-up state."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_2; @(posedge clk) ((vol == N && m) |=> (!m && ((vol == N && sig) || (vol == 0 && !sig)))); endproperty",
      "explanation": "At the upper bound while m is set, the next state clears m. It either holds the high signal for one cycle or resets to zero."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_3; @(posedge clk) ((vol == N && !m) |=> (!m && !sig && ((vol == N-1) || (vol == 0)))); endproperty",
      "explanation": "Once m is clear at the upper bound, the next transition lowers vol and sig, unless reset clears both instead."
    },
    {
      "lemma": "property lemma_4; @(posedge clk) (((vol < N && !m) || (vol == 0)) |=> !sig); endproperty",
      "explanation": "The falling phase cannot raise sig, and a zero-valued vol cannot reach N in one transition. This covers the remaining cycle of the target's two-cycle obligation, including after reset."
    }
  ]
}
</json>

Concurrent assertions sample state before the clocked assignments, and `s_nexttime` starts the target check at the following clock. At the peak, `sig` can remain high for two sampled cycles, but not a third. ([fpga.mit.edu](https://fpga.mit.edu/6205/_static/F25/documentation/1800-2017.pdf))

